MemoryError: BindCraft 2 ran out of device memory in the Evoformer backward at 608 tokens.
  complex   595 residues, padded to 608 tokens (tt-bio buckets the token axis to 32)
  asked for 189.3 MB in one DRAM buffer (15.8 MB in each of 12 banks)
  free      149.3 MB of 12.885 GB, largest contiguous block 2.0 MB
The card is full: 149.3 MB free against a 189.3 MB request, with 12.736 GB of 12.885 GB already held by this fold.
What to do: run a smaller complex. The token axis is the complex BindCraft 2 built, padded to a multiple of 32 -- it is LARGER than target residues + binder length, so size the job off the 595 above and not off that sum. 19 residues off the binder takes this fold to 576 tokens. The largest axis measured to complete a gradient round on one p150a is 576 tokens. Trimming the target to the domain you are binding is the other lever and usually the bigger one.
